# Found Footage: "You may look at face-down creatures your opponents control any time" (CR 708.5). Turn 1 Bot1 casts it. Turn 2
# Bot2 casts Vengeful Creeper face down for its disguise: on the stack it stays hidden from Bot1 (the ruling: face-down spells
# aren't covered), and once it resolves Bot1 knows it is Vengeful Creeper, as its client draws it; Bot2 sees no face of Bot1's.
# Turn 3 Bot1 pays {2} and sacrifices Found Footage: surveil 2 (one Island to the graveyard), then draw a card - and with the
# Clue gone the Creeper is hidden from Bot1 again.

[Bot1 Deck]
Found Footage
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Vengeful Creeper
Forest x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Found Footage.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot2.Hand.Vengeful Creeper.Cast(Ability: Disguise)
? Stack..FaceDown = true
? Bot1.Sees.Bot2.FaceDown =
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield..FaceDown = true
? Bot1.Sees.Bot2.FaceDown = Vengeful Creeper
? Bot2.Sees.Bot1.FaceDown =
? Client.Bot1.OpponentBattlefield.Vengeful Creeper.FaceDownName = Vengeful Creeper
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Found Footage.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Arrange(Island | Island)

[Expect]
Bot1.Sees.Bot2.FaceDown =
Bot1.Graveyard = Island; Found Footage
Bot1.Hand.Count = 6
Bot2.Battlefield..FaceDown = true
